  "term": "prenatal care",
  "definition": "Prenatal care is care received during pregnancy. In this context, it is described as something that can affect satisfaction with care, decisions about seeking care, and health outcomes for both the pregnant parent and the newborn, with experiences shaped by social and health inequities.",
